Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix: show market + BPI data block in confidence UI
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- api/analyze.js: return odds_data field in handler response so frontend
  has raw market context (spread, moneylines, BPI, line movement, futures)

- public/ai-panel.js:
  * renderConfidence now accepts oddsRaw param
  * builds market & BPI section from odds_data string — shows DraftKings
    spread, O/U, home/away moneylines with implied probabilities, opening
    line movement, ESPN BPI win%, predicted margin, matchup quality, futures
  * weights label now reads from conf.weights (dynamic 40/20/20/20)
    instead of hardcoded 50/25/25

- public/style.css: add .conf-market-block, .market-header, .market-row
