From 174f9725719d4620a75a87a5631a0e0119079931 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ncaa-graph-bot <meeraja@ncaa-graph>
Date: Tue, 24 Mar 2026 08:43:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] redesign: bracket-first UI with dedicated odds surface
 and nav routing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Architecture change:
- Bracket is now the default landing view (hero, full viewport)
- Odds is a top-level nav destination with its own dedicated page
- Graph is demoted to a nav tab — still full-featured, just not the homepage
- Rankings gets a full-width 4-column layout, no longer buried in sidebar
- New top nav: Bracket | Odds | Graph | Rankings

Bracket view:
- Full-width scrollable bracket stage replaces dropdown-in-sidebar
- 2x2 regional grid with real bracket tree structure (R64 → Elite Eight)
- Final Four and Championship sections below
- Model selector + Simulate button always visible in sticky control bar
- Bebas Neue display font for all bracket headings

Odds view (new — public/odds.js):
- Three tabs: Upcoming / Completed / Futures
- Game cards with DraftKings spread, O/U, home/away moneylines + implied %
- ESPN BPI win probability bar per game (home% vs away% visual)
- Opening line + line movement note (sharp money signal ≥1.5%)
- Futures: regional winner and championship odds with probability bars
- Groups by date with round badge (Sweet 16, Elite Eight etc)

Graph view:
- All existing graph functionality preserved
- Toolbar simplified to single row with gtb- classes
- Sidebar tabs (Overview / Rankings / Detail / Paths) unchanged

Rankings view:
- 4-column layout: Wins vs Field / T-Rank Efficiency / Underseeded / Overseeded
- Populated from same data, clicking a team switches to Graph and focuses it

CSS:
- Bebas Neue for display headings (year, bracket names, section headers)
- All new components use existing CSS variables (warm neutral palette)
- Responsive: 2-col at 900px, 1-col at 600px
---
